      "trace_id": "scamper-M"
    },
    {
      "operator": "P",
      "operator_name": "Put to other uses",
      "idea": "Use common household items (e.g., waste metal or repurposed plastic drums) as components for a modular, insulated flow-through system that utilizes waste heat generated from community cooking fires (a pervasive energy source) to achieve water pasteurization before consumption, effectively using existing energy infrastructure for disinfection.",
      "trace_id": "scamper-P"
    },
    {
      "operator": "E",
      "operator_name": "Eliminate",
      "idea": "Eliminate all complex operational steps and infrastructure reliance by implementing large-scale, decentralized gravity-driven Bio-Filters combined with Point-of-Use (POU) Ceramic Filtration. The community system only handles pre-treatment and settling, relying entirely on individual, simple, replaceable ceramic filters for the final pathogen barrier, eliminating the need for centralized complex disinfection equipment.",
